--TEST--
inside a string literal at a `string<propertyPath<T>>` parameter, the text after an unclosed `{` is a path written one segment at a time: a `.` after a valid prefix offers the public properties of the class that prefix reaches, and a `{{` before it opens no hole — `rule:ide/a-field-path-completes-one-segment-at-a-time`
--FILE--
<?nvs
class Customer {
    public string $name = "Ada";
    private string $secret = "x";
}
class Order {
    public string $id = "o1";
    public ?Customer $customer = null;
}
class Grid {
    public static function where(string<propertyPath<Order>> $condition): string {
        return $condition as string;
    }
}

echo Grid::where("{{literal}} {id} = 1 and {customer.<|>");
--REQUEST--
completion
--EXPECT--
name    property  string
